OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`.
That path is NOT a project.yml source group (the iOS/macOS app targets list `Sources`
+ `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,
shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled
canonical admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, where the sibling
P7 admin pages (ApiPlayground, AuditLog, DiskForecast, SchemaDrift, LiveSignalInspector,
TeslaOrders, VehicleCost, …) ship and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml
source path. The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the
faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Admin`. Strings ship in the platform
catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the
same reconciliation the sibling AuditLog / DiskForecast / SchemaDrift logs recorded; it
is the only deviation from the literal prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the standalone admin path `/redis-signals`. A dedicated
`.redisSignals` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment `redis-signals`, System group, icon
`cylinder.split.1x2`); `AppRoute.pathSegment` resolves `/redis-signals` to it directly
(`AppRouteParser.parse` first-segment match), and `RedisSignalViewerRouteRegistration`
hosts `RedisSignalViewerPage` on it, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift
right after `LiveSignalInspectorRouteRegistration`. So the page is reachable via the
System-group sidebar entry and any `/redis-signals` deep link. (Navigation registration
is an allowed file per the prompt.)

