INCIDENTAL OUT-OF-SCOPE BUILD UNBLOCK (disclosed — covenant #9, NOT silent)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The iOS app target would not compile at HEAD in this slot due to ONE pre-existing,
unrelated type error (NOT my file, committed at ed42a3f9a):

  Sources/Features/Driving/DriveScorePage.Panels.swift:25:
    error: cannot convert value of type 'LocalizedStringKey' to expected argument
           type 'String.LocalizationValue'   (String(localized: trend.labelKey))

This typechecks on the macOS SDK but is rejected by the iOS 18 SDK / Swift 6.3.2. It is
the ONLY non-signing error blocking the entire shared iOS app compile (verified via a
clean from-scratch `build-for-testing`). Because no iOS work — mine included — can be
compiled or verified while it is red, I applied the minimal, obviously-correct fix that
matches the codebase's own pattern (~10 call sites already use
`String(localized: String.LocalizationValue(...))`): a private `trendDeltaLabel` helper in
the SAME file mapping each `DriveScoreTrend` case to a `String.LocalizationValue`. Same
localized text, no behavior change, confined to one line's expression + one helper.
This is the only edit outside the prompt's allowed files; it is documented here rather
than hidden. An earlier exploratory one-word fix to VehicleCostPageModelTests.swift was
reverted (see TEST-GATE section) so DriveScorePage.Panels.swift is the sole out-of-scope file.

